Pretty intensive presentation course;
Point out all important points in different scenarios;
Quite useful for those people who need to do presentations in their daily works.

On the one side, there are "amazing" advises like
'Don't write
const a = 1;
const b = 2;
because
const a = 1, b = 2; has better performance.'

So far, this course challenges my full attention:
1)  I must repeat over and over again the phrases and sentences so my ear and voice are trained to arrive at perfection;
2)  the Chinese characters are provided with each word and phrase in case I want to train myself to associate the sound/word with its character;
3)  just as presented in the Introduction, my spirit is immersed in the innocence of my early childhood learning songs from my mother.

If you really have never ever programmed with Visual Studio or C#;
If you really never ever have seen an Unity Error;
And if you are not willing to use the google search button, then this is the right course for you.

Short videos that are easy to follow;
Good explanation;
Suitable examples;
All in all, I've learnt a lot :)
